# serial_three_clients_menu -- one region every domain may reach, and only
# one of them may write.
#
# `serial_three_clients.bron` gave three clients a server and no way at all
# to touch each other: every region in it is held by a client and the
# virtualiser, never by two clients, and that privacy is where the room for
# three at once comes from. This declaration adds the one thing a real
# server almost always has and that shape has never carried -- something
# published once and read by everyone.
#
# `menu` is that region. The virtualiser writes it; all three clients hold
# read alone. Nothing else moves: the same four domains, the same three
# channels, the same nine private regions, the same arcs.
#
# What changes is what a reader of the grants can say. Two clients now share
# a region, so any test that asks only WHICH regions a pair touches must
# answer that they conflict -- they may not run at one instant, and they may
# not be reordered. Both answers are wrong, and the document itself says so:
# neither client may write `menu`, so neither can ever see the other's hand
# in it. A region two domains only read is a fact they agree about, not a
# hazard between them.
#
# `menu` carries a direction the way `ask_x` and `back_x` do -- one writer,
# and readers -- so a flow derivation still finds a writer to name. It has
# three readers rather than one, which is exactly what publishing means.
#
# Read whole by `caravan/read.rye`; exercised by `caravan/commute.rye`.

system serial_three_clients_menu

domain serial_virt
domain client_a
domain client_b
domain client_c

channel serial_virt client_a
channel serial_virt client_b
channel serial_virt client_c

region ask_a 4096
region back_a 4096
region taken_a 64
region ask_b 4096
region back_b 4096
region taken_b 64
region ask_c 4096
region back_c 4096
region taken_c 64
region menu 4096

grant ask_a client_a rw
grant ask_a serial_virt r
grant back_a serial_virt rw
grant back_a client_a r
grant taken_a client_a rw
grant ask_b client_b rw
grant ask_b serial_virt r
grant back_b serial_virt rw
grant back_b client_b r
grant taken_b client_b rw
grant ask_c client_c rw
grant ask_c serial_virt r
grant back_c serial_virt rw
grant back_c client_c r
grant taken_c client_c rw
grant menu serial_virt rw
grant menu client_a r
grant menu client_b r
grant menu client_c r
